9ac|n|The hard, calcified tissue of the skeleton of vertebrate animals, consisting very largely of calcic carbonate, calcic phosphate, and gelatine; as, blood and bone. ; One of the pieces or parts of an animal skeleton; as, a rib or a thigh bone; a bone of the arm or leg; also, any fragment of bony substance. (pl.) The frame or skeleton of the body. ; Anything made of bone, as a bobbin for weaving bone lace. ; Two or four pieces of bone held between the fingers and struck together to make a kind of music. ; Dice. ; Whalebone; hence, a piece of whalebone or of steel for a corset. ; Fig.: The framework of anything.	a:6vy,76,1;1gv5,25,3~1gv5,25,3;6vy,76,1	n:6vy,76,1~6vy,76,1	N:1c5l,162,2;252a,65,4;24m6,45,2;2dm8,3,1~252a,65,4;24m6,45,2;1c5l,162,2;2dm8,3,1
